      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In 60-day-old Wistar rats with fetal valproate syndrome, the brain to body weight ratio was higher by 9.4% and activity of dipeptidyl peptidase IV in the serum and cerebrospinal fluid was higher by 18.4 and 40.6%, respectively, than in healthy controls. Activity of prolylendopeptidase in the serum and cerebrospinal fluid in rats with the fetal valproate syndrome did not differ from the control."},
